    {
      "sourceCommit": "fbee1bc9afc3cb471e567f6cdadb12d528de77e6",
      "executableSha256": "1cf5cbcf52a3ec5f9b23ba1041f679d9d8cf1acb22f418028f61abf6331b0348",
      "note": "Adds only the sign-in wording fix for the Docker Hub drive and Share dialogs. Used for the signed-out sign-in, sharing, receiving and personal wording celebration frames."
    }
  ],
  "fixture": "Neutral fixture drives only. Work files: created through the New menu and the Create dialog with storage and cache under C:/mfe-dh-test/captures/fixture, mounted with WinFsp and given neutral text files (Welcome, Meeting notes, Budget 2027, Trip plan, Projects/Plan, Photos/Harbour) through the mounted drive, edited twice for versions; one file deleted for the Recycle Bin. Photos: a New Docker Hub drive in the public test repository mfe-capture-test with two neutral files, backed up three times, then restored through Open drive from Docker Hub. The needs-attention state was produced by moving that drive's storage folder away while it was locked and asking for one backup; the folder was put back afterwards. Shares were made from the fixture drives and revoked afterwards; the revocation was confirmed. The personal wording frames use a synthetic file that renames Drives, History and Recycle Bin.",
  "captureMethod": "Playwright _electron launch of the packaged executable with a fresh isolated --user-data-dir profile and a hidden, unfocusable window; window screenshots at device scale factor 1; theme, density and language set through the Settings controls",
  "privacy": "Every frame was inspected by eye before publishing. Grey boxes (Playwright screenshot masks) cover any text that names the signed-in Docker Hub account, which includes repository names, any user profile folder path, share commands and pasted share commands. Masks can also cover text hidden behind an open dialog. Pixels were never edited otherwise. Frames where a mask did not cover a profile path, or covered the controls of an open dialog, were discarded and recaptured.",
  "notCaptured": [
    "The Docker Hub device sign-in code screen: the signed-out frame was produced with a throwaway home folder that has no Docker credential store, so the panel stops at the credential store message. Reaching the code would mean using the real credential store, which holds the account sign-in.",
    "A backup progress percentage: the test drive is a few kilobytes, so the backing-up frame shows Backing up without a percentage.",
    "Restored drive after unlock inside Open drive from Docker Hub: in that frame the masks for the details pane behind the dialog covered the dialog's Close button, so it was discarded; the unlock frame shows the restored and verified state.",
    "The file context menu with its Share via Docker Hub entry: a pointer-opened menu was closed by the file list's refresh before a frame could be taken, so the context menu frames were opened with Shift+F10 on a focused row, where the menu offered only Customize.",
    "The Finishing backup prompt on quit: it only appears when a backup is still running after the grace period, which the small test drive never reaches; it is covered by test/auto-backup-quit-flush.test.js.",
    "Dark and Cantonese versions of every page: dark covers Home, the workspace, History, the backup page, Local tools, Settings and the unlock bar; Cantonese and bilingual cover Home, the workspace, Settings and the backup page."
  ],
